<DocsLayout title="Haystack guide | dotfetch" description="Integrate dotfetch with the Haystack Agent: tools re-selected every step through Agent hooks, error tool results, approval through ConfirmationHook, and the Agent State.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Framework guide</p>
  <h1>Haystack</h1>
  <p class="lead">dotfetch plugs into the Haystack <code>Agent</code>'s own mechanisms: hooks and a dynamic <code>Toolset</code> that pick each step's tools, error tool results for failures, <code>ConfirmationHook</code> for human approval, and the <code>State</code> for your run data.</p>
  <p><a class="pill" href="/dotfetch/docs/frameworks/haystack/advanced/">Advanced Haystack usage →</a></p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`uv add "dotfetch[haystack]"   # haystack-ai >= 3.0`} />

  <h2>Basic page: tools picked every step</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from dotfetch import DotFetch
from dotfetch.haystack import HaystackAdapter
from haystack.components.generators.chat import OpenAIChatGenerator
from haystack.dataclasses import ChatMessage

fetcher = DotFetch()

@fetcher.register(examples=["where is my order", "has order 4471 shipped"])
def get_order_status(order_id: str) -> str:
    """Return the current shipping status for an order."""
    return "in_transit"

await fetcher.sync()
agent = HaystackAdapter(fetcher).agent(chat_generator=OpenAIChatGenerator(), limit=5)
result = agent.run(messages=[ChatMessage.from_user("Has order 4471 shipped?")])   # or run_async`} />
  <p>For a fixed set, pass <code>Agent(tools=await adapter.select(query))</code> instead.</p>

  <h2>What the model sees when a tool fails</h2>
  <p>A failed call becomes an error tool result with the text <code>"&lt;type&gt;: &lt;message&gt;"</code>, capped at 2,000 characters, so the model can correct a bad argument or try something else.</p>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Redact or opt out:</strong> <code>HaystackAdapter(fetcher, error_formatter=redact)</code> rewrites the text; <code>error_mode="raise"</code> raises the plain <code>ToolExecutionError</code> instead.</div>

  <h2>Reading run state from a dotfetch tool</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from dotfetch.haystack import current_agent_state

@fetcher.register
def get_balance(account: str) -> str:
    """Fetch an account balance for the signed-in user."""
    state = current_agent_state()            # the Agent's State, or None outside a run
    return bank.balance(state.get("user"), account)

# agent = adapter.agent(chat_generator=..., state_schema={"user": {"type": str}})
# agent.run(messages=[...], user="dan")`} />
